      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raju lived in the Sundarbans and spent his days hunting fish. One evening, he smelled something incredible drifting from a nearby village—biryani. He crept closer and watched a grandmother layer rice, meat and spices in a heavy pot. The aroma made him forget all about fish.\n\nThe next day, Raju found an old cookbook washed up on the riverbank. He taught himself to read, then gathered ingredients: rice from a farmer's field, chicken from a coop (he left some rupees behind), and spices from a spice merchant's cart. He built a fire by the river and followed the recipe step by step, his big paws surprisingly gentle with the saffron threads.\n\nWhen the biryani was ready, Raju invited all the forest animals to taste it. The deer, the monkeys, even the crocodiles came. They declared it the best biryani in Bengal. From that day on, Raju opened a small dhaba by the river, where animals and humans ate together in peace, one plate at a time.\n\n5:00 AM",
